    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L12-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Margin of Error for Means",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Similar to estimating proportions for populations, we can estimate a population mean based on the mean of several random samples. Using the data from the samples, find the mean of the sample means and the standard deviation of the sample…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l12.rich-lesson-v2.json",
