    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L12-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "12.3: Margin of Error for Means",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For example, a digital clock maker wants to know how well its clocks keep time. They select several random samples of 40 clocks and compare them to an atomic clock to see how many seconds are lost or gained in a day. From each sample, they…",
